  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 81b9501dec89da64eb81f4c230bdd187, type: 3}
  m_Name: Blessing of Dawn
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HoneyAndHemlock.Customers.CustomerSO
  _requestedPotion: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b5aa1c65083f4da43a4db014123fba7e, type: 2}
  _request:
  - My garden has been dying for months. Nothing grows. The soil feels wrong. Even
    the weeds won't take root. The old wives say something cursed the land. I just
    need something to bring life back to it.
  - The old willow by the Arcane Library has been withering since the frost took
    hold last winter. It's been there longer than anyone can remember. If it dies,
    something bad is coming. I need to save it.
  _playerResponse:
  - Life can be restored
  - Let's bring it back
  _successfulResponse:
  - I poured it into the soil this morning and by midday the first green shoot broke
    through. By evening there were three. Three! After months of nothing, I think
    you just saved my livelihood.
  - New leaves. On a dead tree. The elders are calling it a miracle. I'm calling
    it the best coin I ever spent. Thank you.
  _failedResponse:
  - Something grew alright. But it's not anything I've ever seen before. Black roots,
    silver leaves, and it's growing fast. Very fast. I don't think this is what we
    wanted.
  - The willow woke up. That's the only way I can describe it. The branches moved
    on their own. Toward me. I left very quickly after that.
  _cosmicResponse:
  - "Something was growing toward me in the dark. Something that\u2019s been growing
    forever\u2026 can it help my garden grow?"
  - That thing has probably been there longer than the willow. Longer than anything.
    But that willow needs me now. You said you had something in mind?
